#. ~ Description of terrain "rope fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of rope, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not "
"to go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "barbed wire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of sharp barbed wire.  The more persuasive brother of the "
"wire fence."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "wire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of wire, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not "
"to go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "picket fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of wood, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not "
"to go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A closed metal gate."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden split rail gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden privacy gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system.  It is tall "
"enough to prevent people from seeing into your yard."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden split rail gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden privacy gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system.  The gate is "
"wide open, allowing anything to travel through."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "chickenwire fence post"
#. ~ Description of terrain "fence post"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A couple of posts that can support a fence.  They look lonely without the "
"fence."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "woven wattle fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A flimsy barrier made of woven sticks.  Suitable for small animals."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch "
"is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "locked wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence.  This one has a locked padlock on the latch "
"system.  With the right tools, you could cut the metal fence or pick the "
"lock.  You could also examine the fence to see if it looks climbable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed chickenwire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chickenwire fence with a simple latch system to stay closed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open chickenwire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chickenwire fence with a simple latch system to stay closed.  "
"The latch is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open palisade gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A hanging palisade gate, hoisted by a nearby pulley system.  You probably "
"shouldn't be underneath when it comes down."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "palisade gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A large doorway consisting of long logs cabled together, best used as part "
"of a longer wall.  Can act as a door if some type of pulley system were "
"rigged on an adjacent palisade wall."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden privacy fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A rather stout fence made of planks and fence posts, it is tall enough to "
"prevent people from seeing into your yard."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "split rail fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A rather stout fence made of planks and fence posts, suitable for containing "
"livestock like horses, cows and pigs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A retractable security gate with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A retractable security gate with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch "
"is undone, so the gate has retracted up."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A retractable security gate.  The latch on this one is locked.  With the "
"right tools, you could cut the metal fence or disable the lock."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "guard rail"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A section of metal railing, put in place to prevent people from falling or "
"taking the easy way out."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of metal railing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "glass railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of railing made out of glass."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "cattle feeder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A section of tall steel with a solid base and feed spaces above to allow "
"livestock to reach the contained food."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of wooden railing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal post"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A set of metal posts that can hold more serious fences."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "narrow fence posts"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A set of narrow wooden posts for a woven wattle fence."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A simple metal fence."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed screen door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A simple wooden doorway with screen mesh."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open screen door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A simple wooden doorway with screen mesh.  The door is open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "chain link fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A tall fence made of woven wires.  There aren't any gaps big enough for you "
"to fit through, so you'll have to cut it, climb it, or find a way around."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "chickenwire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A tall, rather flimsy fence made of planks and woven wire, suitable for "
"containing small livestock like chickens."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "screen mesh wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A tall, rather flimsy wall made of planks and screen mesh, suitable for "
"keeping the bugs out."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A waist-high concrete barrier."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "makeshift portcullis"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"An immense gateway cobbled together from various bits of steel and metal "
