#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid "A plain copper ring.  Not very shiny, and not very popular."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "radiation badge"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A plastic badge with an embedded filmstrip.  The text on the badge says the "
"filmstrip changes color as it is exposed to radiation, and never goes back "
"to how it initially looked.  Wear on your lapel so you can notice if it "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "doctor badge"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A plastic name tag marking the wearer as a real doctor of the medical kind."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fancy watch"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A rather large and expensively-made wristwatch.  Tells the time in elegantly "
"wrought gold with silver detailing.  It's really the only timepiece suitable "
"for someone of your exquisitely discerning tastes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "leather cat ears"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A shiny pair of black cat ears on a headband.  It does nothing, but there's "
"no reason not to look good even if no one's looking."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "silver hairpin"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid "A shiny silver hairpin with a tiny bee engraved onto it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tie clip"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid "A shiny silver tie clip, a great match for a necktie."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "beaded bracelet"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A simple bracelet of string and wooden beads.  Also doubles as a set of "
"prayer beads, if you're so inclined."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "copper necklace"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A simple chain of copper, with a clasp in the middle to create a necklace."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "beaded necklace"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A simple necklace made of string and wooden beads.  Also doubles as a set of "
"prayer beads, if you're so inclined."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handmade holy symbol"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid "A simple necklace representing a religious faith."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "beaded earrings"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid "A simple pair of earrings made of string and wooden beads."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wrist watch"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A simple wristwatch on a plastic band.  Tells the time and has an alarm "
"clock feature."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "silver ring"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid "A simple, silver ring."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "small relic"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A small relic from a forgotten saint.  As extraordinary as the world has "
"become, it may have some power yet."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "silver locket"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A small silver locket with a frame inside to store photographs or small "
"objects."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "silver tiara"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid "A sparkling silver tiara adorned with gems."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "collar pin"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A staple accessory for gentlemen.  Keeps your shirt collar in place and "
"provides a more aesthetically pleasing arc to your necktie."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "detective badge"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid "A tarnished golden shield gives an air of authority to the wearer."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "deputy badge"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid "A tarnished silver star gives an air of authority to the wearer."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "gold cufflinks"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A tasteful pair of gold buttons with toggles on the back.  These are meant "
"to be worn in the buttonholes in the cuffs of a dress shirt."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "diver's watch"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"A waterproof, self-winding watch on a stainless steel watchband.  Tells the "
"time and current temperature.  Activate to check the digital thermometer."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of item "holy symbol"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid "Adventist Bible necklace"
msgid_plural "Adventist Bible necklaces"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. ~ Description of "purity ring"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
msgid ""
"Also known as a promise ring, this ring is worn as a sign of chastity.  This "
"one bears the inscription, \"Love is patient.\""
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "hair beads"
#: data/json/items/armor/jewelry.json
