#. ~ Description of "boiled large human stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A boiled stomach from a large humanoid creature, nothing else.  It looks all "
"but appetizing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "large boiled stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A boiled stomach from an animal, nothing else.  It looks all but appetizing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "putrid heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A cartliginous knot of flesh the size of a small pumpkin, superficially "
"resembling a mammalian heart and covered in ribbed grooves.  It's still full "
"of whatever passes for blood in jabberwocks, and is heavy in your hands.  "
"After everything you've seen lately, you can't help but remember old sayings "
"about eating the hearts of your enemies…"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of lung"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A chewy, grayish lump of flavorless connective tissue.  It doesn't look any "
"tastier than it did raw, but any parasites are all cooked out."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of brain from a human.  Eating this may cause kuru, but you probably "
"won't live long enough to care about that anyway."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of brain from an animal.  You wouldn't want to eat this raw…"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked fatty meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of cooked fatty meat.  Although absent of vitamins, it is very "
"filling and delightfully greasy."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of cooked meat.  It's filling and nutritious, but unseasoned and a "
"bit bland."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked lobster"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of delicious cooked lobster meat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human kidney"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of kidney from a human, which appears to have been extracted too "
"crudely to ever be useful as a transplant."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw kidney"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of kidney from an animal.  Preparing it for cooking is a challenge "
"unless you want the kitchen to smell strongly of urine."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "human flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of raw meat, butchered from a human body."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chunk of meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of raw meat.  You could eat it as-is, but cooking it is better."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chunk of lobster meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of uncooked lobster meat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked foul meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A cooked chunk of meat from a mutated animal.  It still looks and smells all "
"wrong."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked fish"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A cooked fish fillet.  Very nutritious."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked human flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A cooked portion of human flesh."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chunk of porkbelly"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A fatty cut of pork from the belly, popular in some cuisine.  With proper "
"technique, it can be used to create bacon.  Not safe to consume in its "
"current raw form."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tainted hide"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A ghastly skin marred by decay.  It sloughs apart like wet newspaper when "
"handled, and the smell is intolerable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "purged gastropods"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A handful of lucky gastropods that have been prepared for cooking by "
"repeatedly boiling and washing them to remove their mucus and pathogens."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "large slab of uncut bacon"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A huge slab of uncut smoked bacon.  You can eat it as is, but it would be "
"more efficient to cut it into smaller portions with a knife."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "pickled offal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A mass of entrails and organ meat, preserved in brine.  Packed with "
"essential vitamins, and although it looks like a lab specimen, it actually "
"tastes pretty palatable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human liver"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A piece of liver from a human, which appears to have been extracted too "
"crudely to ever be useful as a transplant."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw liver"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A piece of liver from an animal.  Although many dislike its texture, it's "
"one of the more vitamin-rich parts of the animal.  It is very good in "
"sausages, but maybe a little less appetizing when cooked on its own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chunk of tainted meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A piece of meat that's obviously unhealthy.  You could eat it, but it will "
"poison you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chunk of mi-go flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A piece of spongelike pink flesh.  It's nearly as hard as wood at its core, "
"with an armored crust lining the exterior.  The smell suggests it is "
"definitely not edible."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human sweetbread"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A piece of the thymus or pancreas of a human, which appears to have been "
"extracted too crudely to ever be useful as a transplant."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw sweetbread"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A piece of the thymus or pancreas of an animal.  These are a delicacy, if "
"prepared properly."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A portion of an animal's heart.  It's tough but not that chewy, and it "
"spoils very quickly."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A portion of heart from a human.  It's tough but not that chewy, and it "
"spoils very quickly.  It appears to have been extracted too crudely to ever "
"be useful as a transplant."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human lung"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A portion of lung from a human.  It's spongy and pink, and spoils very "
"quickly.  It appears to have been extracted too crudely to ever be useful as "
"a transplant."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw lung"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A portion of lung from an animal.  It's spongy and pink, and spoils very "
"quickly.  It can be a delicacy if properly prepared - but if improperly "
"prepared, it's a chewy lump of flavorless connective tissue."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "frog legs"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A raw pair of frog legs.  Tastes like chicken when cooked or smoked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "raw pelt"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A raw skin harvested from a fur-bearing animal.  You can cure it for storage "
"and tanning, or scrape the fur off to get a clean hide."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "raw human pelt"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A raw skin harvested from a fur-bearing mutant human.  It still has the fur "
"attached.  You can cure it for storage and tanning, or eat it if you're "
"desperate enough."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "raw hide"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A raw skin harvested from an animal.  You can cure it for storage and "
"tanning, or eat it if you're desperate enough."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "desiccated putrid heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A red-black strip of muscle - all that remains of a putrid heart that has "
"been sliced open and drained of blood.  It could be eaten if you're hungry, "
"but looks *disgusting*."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A roasted piece of heart.  It doesn't look any tastier than it did raw, but "
"any parasites are all cooked out."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tainted limb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A rotted and then shredded arm.  Not much use unless you want to scrape the "
"meat from the bones."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tainted pelt"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A rotting pelt from some long-dead furry creature.  It's already too far "
"gone to be tanned, and rapidly getting worse."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked mutant bug organs"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A selection of cooked mutant bug organs.  Looks awful, but if you give it a "
"try, you'll find -- that it's worse than it looks."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked offal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A selection of cooked organs and entrails.  Filled with essential vitamins, "
"but pretty unappetizing in this form."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "raw offal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A selection of uncooked internal organs and entrails.  Filled with essential "
"vitamins, but most people consider it a bit gross unless it's very carefully "
"prepared."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chunk of tainted human meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A slab of human flesh that stinks to high heaven.  The tissue is breaking "
"down far too quickly."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "boiled human stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A small boiled stomach from a human, nothing else.  It looks all but "
"appetizing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "boiled stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A small boiled stomach from an animal, nothing else.  It looks all but "
"appetizing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "portion of raw bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A soft, spongy substance found in bones, rich in fat.  Chock-full of good "
"stuff and doesn't taste too bad even raw, but beware of parasites."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "seeping heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A thick mass of flesh superficially resembling a mammalian heart.  It's the "
"size of your fist and covered in dimpled grooves."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked scrap of foul meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A tiny scrap of cooked meat from a mutated animal.  It still smells "
"unappealing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "scrap of fish"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A tiny scrap of edible fish.  It's not much, but it'll do in a pinch."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "scrap of human flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A tiny scrap of raw human flesh."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "scrap of foul meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A tiny scrap of raw meat from a heavily mutated animal.  It smells "
"unappealing, to say the least."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "scrap of meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A tiny scrap of raw meat.  It's not much, but it'll do in a pinch."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "portion of tainted bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A wet, green chunk of spongy goop extracted from a rotten bone.  It looks "
"and smells all wrong."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "portion of tainted bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"A wet, green chunk of spongy goop extracted from a rotten bone.  You could "
"eat it, but it will poison you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fillet of fish"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "An uncooked fish fillet.  Makes a passable meal raw."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tainted innards"
#. ~ Description of "tainted human innards"
#. ~ Snippet in category "tainted_innards_desc"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
#: data/json/snippets/zombie_anatomy.json
msgid ""
"An unidentifiable selection of rotted innards that barely hold their form.  "
"It is revolting and certainly no longer healthy to eat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mutant blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Blood extracted from a heavily mutated creature."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mutant human blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Blood extracted from a heavily mutated human."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "human blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Blood extracted from a human being."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "animal blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Blood extracted from a living creature."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "roasted bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Bone marrow, fully cooked to eliminate any parasites.  Tasty!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of liver"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Chock-full of A- and B-Vitamins!  Cooked liver isn't all that bad, depending "
"on how you feel about the texture, but this is probably the least fancy way "
"to do it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked gastropods"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Cooked gastropods.  A bit low on calories, but high in protein."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked cretin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Cooked meat from a heavily mutated humanoid.  Now that the worst bits have "
"been picked out, it's probably digestible, if not very appetizing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked mollusk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Cooked mollusk meat.  Devoid of any parasites or bacteria due to heat, the "
"only thing left to do is add sauce."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "canned offal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Cooked organ meat and entrails, preserved by canning.  Unappetizing, but "
"filled with essential vitamins."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fried meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Delicious oil-fried meat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "butchery refuse"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Eugh.  This is a mess of dirt, excreta, connective tissue, and bits of "
"matter like hair and claws, leftover from the butchering process.  Eating it "
"isn't even worth thinking about."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "smoked fish"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Fish that has been heavily smoked for long term preservation.  It could be "
"further smoked to dehydrate it completely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tainted blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Foul blood that's rapidly getting worse.  Separated from its owner, it seems "
"intent on congealing into a disgusting jelly as fast as possible.  You could "
"drink it, but it will poison you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tainted human blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Foul human blood that's rapidly getting worse.  Separated from its owner, it "
"seems intent on congealing into a disgusting jelly as fast as possible."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mi-go ichor"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Goo from inside a mi-go, perhaps some kind of blood?  It's obviously alien, "
"given its pink color and strange, nostril-stinging odor.  It would not be "
"advisable to try to drink it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "smoked lobster"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Lobster that has been heavily smoked for long term preservation.  It could "
"be further smoked to dehydrate it completely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "smoked meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Meat that has been heavily smoked for preservation.  It could be further "
"smoked to dehydrate it completely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "smoked mollusk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Mollusk meat that has been heavily smoked for long term preservation.  It "
"could be further smoked to dehydrate it completely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of kidney"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "No, this is not beans."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of sweetbread"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Normally a delicacy, but this style of preparation is missing something."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Now you can emulate those zombies you love so much!  Preparing brain for "
"eating is challenging, and this doesn't seem to be the best way to do it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "slab of raw curing porkbelly"
#. ~ Description of "slab of raw curing porkbelly (obsolete)"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
#: data/json/obsoletion_and_migration/obsoletion.json
msgid ""
"Porkbelly in the process of becoming fully cured with salt and sugar, "
"capable of becoming bacon.  The flavor is slowly developing at this stage, "
"and is significantly unpleasant due to the residual salt.  Activate it once "
"completed to make use of the final product."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "slab of raw cured porkbelly"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Porkbelly that has been preserved and flavored with salt and sugar to draw "
"out the moisture from the first layer.  Still raw, it is ready for smoking "
"into bacon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mutant humanoid meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Raw meat butchered from the body of a heavily mutated creature that was "
"unsettlingly humanoid in appearance.  It has odd bits of fur and other "
"tissue lodged in it that clearly don't belong.  You'd have to be crazy or "
"starving to eat this."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chunk of foul meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Raw meat obviously taken from a heavily mutated animal.  It looks and smells "
"all wrong."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mutant organs"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Raw organs from a giant mutant bug."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "smoked tainted mutant meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Rotten mutant meat that has been heavily smoked for preservation."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "meat jerky"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Salty dried meat that lasts for a long time, but will make you thirsty."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tainted skin scraps"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Shredded scraps of raw skin from an unnatural creature.  It can't have much "
"use."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "portion of raw mutant bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Soft, spongy and oddly-colored marrow tissue from the bone of a heavily "
"mutated animal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "portion of raw mutant human bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"Soft, spongy and oddly-colored marrow tissue from the bone of a heavily "
"mutated creature that was unsettlingly humanoid in appearance."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "portion of raw human bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Soft, spongy marrow tissue from a human bone."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "raw human skin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"The flayed hide of a human being.  You can cure it for storage and tanning, "
"or eat it if you're desperate enough."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fillet of mollusk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The raw flesh of a mollusk.  Must be cleaned and cooked before eating."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "human stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a human.  It is surprisingly durable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mutant human stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a large humanoid creature.  It is surprisingly durable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "large mutant stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a large mutated creature.  It is surprisingly durable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "large stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a large woodland creature.  It is surprisingly durable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mutant stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid ""
"The stomach of a mutated creature.  It is clearly malformed and smells "
"revolting."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a woodland creature.  It is surprisingly durable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tainted limb"
#. ~ Snippet in category "leg_zed_desc"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
#: data/json/snippets/zombie_anatomy.json
msgid ""
"What's left of some zombie's limb.  Most likely a leg based on the "
"proportions.  Though it's rotted, there is quite a bit of meat still on it."
msgstr ""

