#. ~ Description of "cestus"
#: data/json/items/melee/unarmed_weapons.json
msgid ""
"A leather hand and arm wrap incorporating metal plates over the knuckles to "
"improve punching power and defense."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "scrap knuckles"
#: data/json/items/melee/unarmed_weapons.json
msgid ""
"A mass of scrap metal crudely beat into shape, with folded rags underneath "
"to protect the wearer's knuckles."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "studded gloves"
#: data/json/items/melee/unarmed_weapons.json
msgid "A pair of gloves with studded metal knuckles and a thin back plating."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "nail knuckles"
#: data/json/items/melee/unarmed_weapons.json
msgid ""
"A pair of knuckles consisting of two small squares of wood with several "
"nails sticking through them.  Useful in nasty street fights."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "steel knuckles"
#: data/json/items/melee/unarmed_weapons.json
msgid ""
"A pair of knuckles forged from steel, designed to be worn over the fingers "
"to cause punches to do more damage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "skewer knuckles"
#: data/json/items/melee/unarmed_weapons.json
msgid ""
"A pair of metal braces, each with a single sturdy spike attached.  When "
"strapped to your hands, the spikes protrude 5 centimeters past your clenched "
"fists."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "impact knuckles"
#: data/json/items/melee/unarmed_weapons.json
msgid "A pair of thick steel plates to wear over the knuckles."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bagh nakh"
#: data/json/items/melee/unarmed_weapons.json
msgid ""
"Also called tiger claws, these Indian weapons consist of two sets of finger "
"rings that secure curved steel claws to the wearer's palms, allowing for "
"vicious unarmed attacks while worn."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "brass knuckles"
#: data/json/items/melee/unarmed_weapons.json
msgid ""
"Two sets of metal rings connected to lugs which are worn over the fingers to "
"add a good deal of power to the user's punches."
msgstr ""

