#. ~ Description of "swage and die set"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A big steel block with various holes and grooves in it, accompanied by some "
"oddly-shaped metal pegs.  These items are essential for shaping metal during "
"the forging process."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bronze anvil"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A block of oddly-shaped bronze complete with a pritchel hole and hardy "
"hole.  Once installed, it can be used in most metalworking fabrication "
"recipes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "finished charcoal kiln"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A charcoal kiln that has finished burning.  Disassemble it to get the "
"charcoal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "crude bronze nail"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A crude bronze nail.  Probably not useful for many things due to its size "
"and shape."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "gas forge"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A gas-fueled metalworking forge.  With the right tools, you could use this "
"for metalworking."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "hotcut"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A hardened chisel-like object for metalsmithing.  It's used to cut lengths "
"of metal in some metalworking fabrication recipes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "drift"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A hardened spike-like object for metalsmithing.  It's used to make holes in "
"metal in some metalworking fabrication recipes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "steel scraper"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A hardened steel tool similar to a drawknife, but for metal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "anvil"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A heavy block of oddly-shaped steel complete with a pritchel hole and hardy "
"hole.  Once installed, it can be used in most metalworking fabrication "
"recipes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "filled charcoal kiln"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A kiln filled with wood which will become charcoal after a slow period of "
"burning."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "lit charcoal kiln"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A kiln full of wood that has been lit; better drop it!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "large sandcasting mold"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A large mold for casting molten metals into different shapes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "polishing stone"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A large natural stone with a flat surface to grind against."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bolt cutters"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A large pair of bolt cutters.  You could use them to cut padlocks or heavy "
"gauge wire."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "long sandcasting mold"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A large, long, mold for casting molten metals into different shapes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sandcasting mold"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A medium mold for casting molten metals into different shapes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "flatjaw tongs"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A pair of flatjaw tongs.  They are commonly used for metalworking, "
"fabrication, or forging recipes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "kitchen tongs"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A pair of long, metal tongs.  They are commonly used for cooking."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sandleather"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A patch of leather paired with a handful of sand.  Works as a substitute for "
"sandpaper."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "draw plate"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A piece of metal with holes of varying size drilled into it.  Used as part "
"of wire drawing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "charcoal forge"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A portable, charcoal-fired metalworking forge.  With the right tools, you "
"could use this for metalworking."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "belt grinder"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A power tool used for grinding and shaping metal or even wood.  It consists "
"of a motorized abrasive belt that spins at high speeds, allowing you to "
"quickly polish, flatten, or overall remove material from surfaces."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "clay crucible"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A primitive metalworking crucible made of clay.  Looks like a stout drink "
"tumbler.  You could use it for metalworking."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "small anvil"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A proper, albeit small, anvil.  Pretty handy."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "pedal powered grindstone"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A round, pedal-powered grindstone, useful for grinding metal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chainmail sheet"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of riveted chainmail.  With some skill, several of these sheets "
"could be connected to make effective armor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sandpaper"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of rough paper.  It is commonly used in metalworking and carpentry."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bronze chisel"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A short, stout metalworking chisel made of bronze.  It's used in some "
"metalworking fabrication recipes.  Bronze chisels spark less than their "
"steel counterparts, but are less durable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "metalworking chisel"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A short, stout metalworking chisel.  It's used in some metalworking "
"fabrication recipes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "jeweler's blowtorch"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A small butane blow torch with a pipe to blow into. Used by jewelers to weld "
"soft metals like gold and copper together."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "crucible"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A small metalworking crucible.  Looks like a stout drink tumbler.  It's used "
"in some metalworking fabrication recipes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "small sandcasting mold"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A small mold for casting molten metals into different shapes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "charcoal kiln"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A stout metal box used for producing charcoal via pyrolysis: the incomplete "
"burning of organic materials in the absence of oxygen."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "blow lamp"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A very early version of a blow torch. Made with a clay bowl that holds a "
"wick and metal tube, it is used by blowing through it to create a precise "
"flame hot enough to weld soft metals like copper and gold. Mainly used for "
"jewelry."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "heavy anvil"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"An absolutely enormous block of oddly-shaped steel with all the bells and "
"whistles a blacksmith could ask for on an anvil.  Necessary for heavy-duty "
"metalworking or dropping on roadrunners."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "electric forge"
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"An electric metalworking forge, powered by your electric grid.  With the "
"right tools, you could use this for metalworking."
msgstr ""

